"\n\n\n\n\n\n## Review\n\nOn the way back home, we wanted to spend some relaxing time, so we searched for a cafe and visited.  \n\nWhen we arrived, it turned out to be a much larger cafe than expected, and we were surprised by the massive number of parked cars.  \nIt was crowded enough to have parking attendants on duty, and the parking lot was already completely full.  \n\nThe cafe appeared to be divided into three separate buildings, and there were plenty of outdoor tables.  \nThe view was wonderful, so if the weather hadn't been so hot, sitting outdoors would have been lovely.  \n\nAfter wandering around for a while to find a seat, we were lucky enough to grab a good indoor spot.  \n\nSince we visited without having lunch, we ordered two bakery items and coffee.  \nThere were many varieties of bread, and we picked two that looked particularly delicious.  \nFor coffee, we ordered an Iced Americano and a Cold Brew.  \n\nPerhaps because they were accustomed to high volumes of guests, the order was prepared without taking very long.  \n\nNext to the pick-up counter, there was a toaster oven to warm up the bread.  \nIt was easy to use, which was convenient.  \n\nAfter warming the bread in the oven, we returned to our table and enjoyed our relaxing time.  \nIt was a great cafe where you could leisurely people-watch and spend a tranquil afternoon.  \n\n## Pictures\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"